{
  "concept": "For 0 < x < π/2, the sector of the unit circle is sandwiched between an inscribed triangle of area sin x / 2 and a circumscribed triangle of area tan x / 2, which forces cos x ≤ sin x / x ≤ 1/cos x and, by the Squeezing Theorem, lim_{x→0} sin x / x = 1.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Left panel: x- and y-axes with arrowheads, origin at center",
    "Left panel: blue unit circle centered at origin",
    "Left panel: red radius from origin to the point (cos x, sin x) on the circle, extended to (1, tan x)",
    "Left panel: red point marker at (1, 0) with label '(1, 0)'",
    "Left panel: red point marker at (cos x, sin x) with leader arrow and label '(cos x, sin x)'",
    "Left panel: red point marker at (1, tan x) with label '(1, tan x)'",
    "Left panel: dashed red chord from (cos x, sin x) to (1, 0)",
    "Left panel: dashed red vertical segment from (1, 0) up to (1, tan x)",
    "Left panel: blue arc on the circle from (1,0) to (cos x, sin x)",
    "Left panel: small angle arc with arrow at the origin labeled 'x'",
    "Left panel: horizontal brace under the segment from origin to (1,0) labeled '1'",
    "Right panel A: large right triangle, pink fill, red outline, base labeled '1', vertical leg labeled 'tan x', dashed blue arc of the unit circle cutting across it, angle mark 'x' at the vertex",
    "Right panel B: circular sector, pink fill, red straight edges, blue curved arc, base labeled '1', angle mark 'x'",
    "Right panel C: small triangle inscribed in the sector, pink fill, red outline, dashed red vertical altitude labeled by a brace 'sin x', dashed blue arc bulging outside the triangle, base labeled '1', angle mark 'x'",
    "Caption row: 'Area of triangle  ≥  Area of sector  ≥  Area of triangle'",
    "Formula row: 'tan x / 2  ≥  x / 2  ≥  sin x / 2'",
    "Derived inequality annotation: 'cos x ≤ sin x / x ≤ 1 / cos x'",
    "Numeric readout box showing current values of tan x / 2, x / 2, sin x / 2, and sin x / x"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "angleX",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "angle x (radians)",
      "range": [0.05, 1.5, 0.01],
      "default": 0.9,
      "teaches": "Sweeping x rigidly links the unit-circle construction to the three areas: the outer triangle always contains the sector, which always contains the inner triangle, no matter how the angle changes."
    },
    {
      "id": "overlayView",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Layout",
      "options": ["Side by side", "Overlaid"],
      "default": "Side by side",
      "teaches": "When the three shapes are stacked on a common vertex and base, the nesting sin-triangle ⊂ sector ⊂ tan-triangle becomes literally visible rather than inferred from separate pictures."
    },
    {
      "id": "regionFocus",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Clicking a panel label isolates one region and its area formula, connecting each picture to the exact term tan x / 2, x / 2, or sin x / 2 in the inequality chain."
    },
    {
      "id": "squeezeStep",
      "type": "state",
      "label": "Proof stage",
      "states": ["Areas", "Divide by sin x / 2", "Take reciprocals", "Squeeze as x→0"],
      "default": "Areas",
      "teaches": "The algebraic chain from the geometric inequality to cos x ≤ sin x / x ≤ 1/cos x, and why letting x→0 pins the middle quantity to 1."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The unit-circle construction",
      "narration": "A single angle x produces three objects on the unit circle: the point (cos x, sin x), the point (1, tan x) on the tangent line, and the arc between them. Drag the angle slider and watch all three move together.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.9, "overlayView": "Side by side", "squeezeStep": "Areas" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Three areas, one angle",
      "narration": "The same angle defines the big triangle (area tan x / 2), the sector (area x / 2), and the small triangle (area sin x / 2). The numeric readout updates as you move x.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.9, "overlayView": "Side by side", "squeezeStep": "Areas" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Overlay: the nesting is literal",
      "narration": "Stacking the three shapes on the same vertex shows the small triangle inside the sector inside the big triangle — containment, not coincidence, is what forces tan x / 2 ≥ x / 2 ≥ sin x / 2.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.9, "overlayView": "Overlaid", "squeezeStep": "Areas" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Divide through by sin x / 2",
      "narration": "Dividing the area inequality by sin x / 2 gives 1/cos x ≥ x / sin x ≥ 1; taking reciprocals flips it to cos x ≤ sin x / x ≤ 1/cos x.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.6, "overlayView": "Overlaid", "squeezeStep": "Take reciprocals" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Squeeze as x → 0",
      "narration": "Shrink x toward zero: the outer and inner shapes collapse onto each other, cos x and 1/cos x both approach 1, and sin x / x is trapped between them — so the limit must be 1.",
      "state": { "angleX": 0.07, "overlayView": "Overlaid", "squeezeStep": "Squeeze as x→0" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The sector's area is trapped between two triangles built from the same angle, so as x→0 the bounds cos x and 1/cos x both close on 1 and drag sin x / x with them.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two-zone layout. Left zone: black axes with arrowheads and origin centered; a blue unit circle; a red ray from the origin through the circle point (cos x, sin x) continuing to (1, tan x) on the vertical tangent line at x = 1; red dot markers at (1,0), (cos x, sin x), (1, tan x) with black serif labels, the middle one attached by a short leader arrow; dashed red chord from (cos x, sin x) to (1,0) and dashed red vertical segment from (1,0) to (1, tan x); the arc from (1,0) to the circle point drawn thicker in blue; a small curved angle arrow at the origin labeled x; a downward brace under the unit radius labeled 1. Right zone: three shapes in a row, all pink-filled with red outlines, all sharing a horizontal base labeled 1 and a small angle arrow labeled x at the left vertex — (a) tall right triangle with vertical right leg labeled 'tan x' and a dashed blue arc cutting through it, (b) circular sector with a solid blue curved outer edge, (c) short triangle whose slanted right edge is the chord, with a dashed blue arc bulging outside it and a right-side brace labeled 'sin x' against a dashed red altitude. Beneath the row, two centered text lines in serif: 'Area of triangle ≥ Area of sector ≥ Area of triangle' and 'tan x/2 ≥ x/2 ≥ sin x/2', aligned under their respective shapes. In overlaid mode the three shapes are drawn concentrically on one vertex with distinct fill opacities (tan-triangle lightest outline-only, sector mid pink, sin-triangle darkest) so nesting reads instantly. Clicked region highlights in saturated red-orange while others fade to grey, with its formula callout enlarged. A small readout panel shows live numeric values of the three areas and sin x / x. Proof-stage text appears as an extra annotation line below the formula row."
}

